        "link": "https://world.digimoncard.com/rule/?card_no=BT6-044#qaResult_card",
        "num": 1,
        "text": "Official English Q&A for BT6-044 (Mar. 28, 2024)"
      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "No, this card’s [When Digivolving] effect reads “you may,” so you can choose whether or not to trash the top card of your security stack.",
        "question": "Does this card’s [When Digivolving] effect force me to trash the top card of my security stack?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "No. You must trash a card from your security stack in order to activate it.",
        "question": "Can I activate this card’s [When Digivolving] effect when my security stack is empty?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, it does.",
        "question": "I use this card’s [When Digivolving] effect to trash a card from my security stack. If there are 3 or fewer cards left in my security stack, does this card’s [All Turns] effect trigger?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Fundamentally, this is possible. However, the effects don’t activate simultaneously, but one at a time in order. Once <Recovery> results in you having 4 cards in your security stack, any remaining copies of the effect don't activate.  Any [BT6-044 Dynasmon] whose effects don’t activate can still be activated later in the turn.",
        "question": "I have 2 or more copies of this Digimon in play. My opponent attacks with a Digimon, removing a card from my security stack. Do all of the effects on copies of this Digimon activate simultaneously, activating <Recovery +1 (Deck)> for each one?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "The [Security] effect activates first.   After the [Security] effect and any effects triggered by its activation have finished activating, this card’s [All Turns] effect activates.",
        "question": "An opponent’s Digimon performs a security check, flipping over a card with a [Security] effect. Which activates first: This card’s [All Turns] effect, or the [Security] effect?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
  },
